Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; Benchy: name the Benchy server for every user of a computer (an example for administrators; no ADMX needed).
;
; Import it on each computer, or push the same two values with Group Policy Preferences (Computer Configuration >
; Preferences > Windows Settings > Registry), or from a deploy script: reg import benchy-server-policy.example.reg
; It needs administrator rights, because it writes under HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE.
;
; Server (text): the server's address, https://host:port, for example your server's name from its certificate. The port is
;   39443 when left out. Benchy lists this server first and preselects it, marked as set by the administrator. It is a
;   starting point only: nothing is paired by it, and a person still types the join code from the server's Systems page.
; DisableDiscovery (number): 1 stops Benchy searching the network (DNS and mDNS), so only this server and an address a
;   person types are used. Leave it out, or use 0, to let Benchy search as usual.
;
; Change the address below, delete the lines you do not want, and keep the key name as it is.

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Benchy]
"Server"="https://benchy.example.com:39443"
"DisableDiscovery"=dword:00000000
